{"shortDescription":"Hungary's forint was a touch lower on Friday, but mostly holding on to gains from the previous session when it was boosted by a Bloomberg report that the central bank would pause rate cuts at its next meeting.The forint FX:EURHUF was 0.2% lower, trading at 363.50 to the euro after gaining around 1…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Hungary's forint was a touch lower on Friday, but mostly holding on to gains from the previous session when it was boosted by a Bloomberg report that the central bank would pause rate cuts at its next meeting."]},{"type":"p","children":["The forint ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX:EURHUF","text":"FX:EURHUF"}}," was 0.2% lower, trading at 363.50 to the euro after gaining around 1.5% in the previous session."]},{"type":"p","children":["Bloomberg said on Thursday the bank would hold its policy rate at 5.5% at its September 22 meeting as it prepares to lower its 3% inflation target to 2.5% — part of Hungary's efforts to join the euro."]},{"type":"p","children":["In response to Reuters questions about the report, the bank said that it will decide on the future path of interest rates based on its September inflation projection."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"The FX market clearly liked the news. The forint rallied sharply intraday after the report, gaining the most since the post-election move in April,\" Commerzbank wrote in a note."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"MNB cutting rates during a period of external inflation risk had become the main source of vulnerability for HUF,\" they said."]},{"type":"p","children":["Elsewhere, the Polish zloty ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"OANDA:EURPLN","text":"OANDA:EURPLN"}}," was up 0.1%, trading at 4.3199 to the euro."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"On Friday, the zloty will remain primarily influenced by impulses from the dollar market. The key release will be the US labor market report,\" analysts at PKO Bank wrote."]},{"type":"p","chi